Looking at the three failures, two are projection-width errors (sp0755 returns only `Name` where gold returns all country columns; sp0536's repair prompt actively pushes `SELECT T1.*` when the question asks for three specific name columns) and one is a wrong join key that silently yields 0 rows (sp0894 guesses `student_id`/`friend_id` instead of the real Friend columns). The incumbent's literal-only samples never show the actual column names or the values of filtered columns, so the repair call cannot fix either class. I'll upgrade the diagnostics to schema-derived: exact stored-value probes per string literal (generic, no hard-coded literals), full referenced-table schemas plus value profiles of filtered columns, and FK edges between referenced tables — plus rewrite the projection guidance in both prompts to be direction-neutral ("which X" → full row; explicitly enumerated attributes → exactly those).

